@@text
@@text Creative Common 1.2.0 of 2026-11-14 (installed), with Creative Delight rebuilt so its salt member no longer melts by
@@text block tick. Group A superflat unless noted; `gamerule randomTickSpeed 1000` for every melt row (`-04` counts steps, so
@@text note the speed), back to 3 for SQ-MELT-P1. Each case gets its own spot at least 12 blocks from the others; probe the
@@text end state with `execute if block`. Config keys are in `config/creativecommon-common.toml` `[melting]` (added by Forge
@@text on the first boot; `grep` before a `qrun.py toml` edit).
@@text
@@table
## SQ-MELT-01 | salt melts touching ice to a water source, snow block / powder snow / layer to air; salt stays
@group A
@commands `setblock X -60 Z salt:salt_block`; around it (touching): `minecraft:ice`, `minecraft:snow_block`, `minecraft:powder_snow`, `minecraft:snow[layers=3]` (layer on a stone block beside the salt); wait 60 s
@pass ice -> `minecraft:water[level=0]`, the other three -> air; the Salt Block stays; latest.log `[melting] tags:` line with salt >= 2
@fails `#creativecommon:melting/salt` empty (`melting_tags.js`, `has('salt')`); snow block and powder snow not melting: `[melting] random ticks on for N extra blocks` missing or N < 4 (`extraRandomTickBlocks`)
@from batches/r1115/p3_a1.qb
> execute if block 2001 -61 2000 minecraft:water[level=0] run say SQ-MELT-01-ice_water
> execute if block 1999 -61 2000 minecraft:air run say SQ-MELT-01-snowblock_air
> execute if block 2000 -61 2001 minecraft:air run say SQ-MELT-01-powder_air
> execute if block 2000 -61 1999 minecraft:air run say SQ-MELT-01-layer_air
> execute if block 2000 -61 2000 salt:salt_block run say SQ-MELT-01-salt_kept
expect SQ-MELT-01-ice_water$
expect SQ-MELT-01-snowblock_air$
expect SQ-MELT-01-powder_air$
expect SQ-MELT-01-layer_air$
expect SQ-MELT-01-salt_kept$
bootexpect \[melting\] tags: \d+ meltable, \d+ slow, ([2-9]|\d\d+) salt
look and the m01_ changes in P3-01's log (one step each); [melting] tags salt >= 2
shell grep -hE "\[zmelt\] change m01_" logs/latest.log | sed -E 's/^.*\[zmelt\]/[zmelt]/'

## SQ-MELT-02 | fire, soul fire, lit campfire, lit soul campfire, magma: ice and snow at 3 melt, at 4 not; unlit campfire nothing
@group A
@commands In a lit room (one torch-free row): ice at distance 3 from `minecraft:fire` (on netherrack) and at distance 4 from a second fire; the same pair for `soul_fire` (on soul soil), `campfire[lit=true]`, `soul_campfire[lit=true]`, `magma_block`; plus ice 1 from `campfire[lit=false]`; wait 90 s
@pass every distance-3 ice melted, every distance-4 ice still ice (each pair); the unlit-campfire ice still ice
@fails the 4-block ice melted: range wrong or vanilla light melt on (`vanillaLightMelting`); magma at 3 not melting: SQ-MELT-07; unlit campfire melting: `fireActive` (lit property)
