## SQ-MELT-09 | Common + Compat: fire and lava melt as in -02 / -03; [melting] tags salt 0; no melting error or warning
@group A
@commands Boot the Common + Compat set (no Creative Delight, so no Salt or Vintage); fire and lava cases of -02 and -03 (one pair each); grep latest.log for `melting`
@pass fire and lava melt as in -02 / -03; `[melting] tags:` with salt 0; no error or warning naming melting
@fails `melting_tags.js` touching an absent mod's id without `has()`; a Java reference to a Salt class
@from batches/r1115/p3_c1.qb
bootexpect \[melting\] tags: \d+ meltable, \d+ slow, 0 salt
# Forge fills a fresh config with "Incorrect key melting... corrected" WARN lines (no config/ in this set): not a fault
bootreject (?i)(ERROR|WARN)(?!.*Incorrect key).*melting|melting.*(Exception|NoClassDefFound)
shell grep -hiE "melting" logs/latest.log | sed -E 's/^.*\]: //' | cut -c1-300 | head -12
